Pomelo v4 on top of the v3 series.

DevTools on Android is allowed to dock, and opening it stores a bottom dock.
Sync accepts "local" for Chromium's on-device backend, which does not need a
Google account, or a custom server URL.

The ad blocker parses ABP/uBlock network filters (||host^, @@ exceptions, and
comments). A starter list ships in the patch. Extra rules pasted in Filter
lists, including rules copied from EasyList, are parsed the same way. EasyList
and uBlock Origin are not bundled.

More tools toggles the desktop site for the current host, reader text size,
translate, print/save as PDF, force zoom, a custom user agent, back and
forward, grouping this tab with a neighbor, and an Incognito PIN.

